  "note": "Baseline shape of a whole-controller export (TargetType=Controller, ContainsContext=false). Establishes the FQN notation the other L5X fixtures assume: a program is its bare name, a routine is <Program>.<Routine>, a controller-scoped tag is its bare name, and a program-scoped tag is <Program>.<Tag>. Read and write edges are attributed to the owning routine, not to the rung, because the routine is the chunk unit (plcHandoff.md, 'What is decided'). Rungs stay addressable as sub-units but are not themselves symbols.",
